WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
A cyclist rides out of
town, into a head wind,

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.340
at ten kilometres per hour.

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.770
Coming home, the wind is behind her.

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.840
Thirty kilometres per hour.

5
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.700
Her friend says: ten plus
thirty, divided by two.

6
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.560
So you averaged twenty.

7
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.550
Is that right?

8
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.010
Exactly twenty?

9
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.640
Or could it be more, or less?

10
00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:25.330
In this mission, you'll use time
equals distance divided by speed.

11
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.230
Each leg's time becomes a
fraction, like d over ten.

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.690
You'll add algebraic fractions
over a common denominator.

13
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.760
Never by adding the bottoms.

14
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.780
And you'll work out average
speed for a whole journey,

15
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.670
from its total distance and total time.

16
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.300
Your mission: work out whether your
average speed really is twenty kilometres

17
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.030
per hour.
